From 39e1437d52dd1c0f65e1b34ed23847caa13c248a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 17:01:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 198/199] hir_typeck: a method call allocates value ivars for
 in-scope traits with const params

The method-call node keeps a pool of type ivars for the in-scope traits
that provide the method, so each find_method pass searches with the same
`Trait<_, ..>` params. Traits with const params had no such pool and the
lookup asserted: "TODO: Handle value params" (helpers.cpp
get_ivared_params) for `self.hist.volume(cube)` in quantette 0.6.0
quantize/wu/shared.rs with `InclusionExclusion<T, const N: usize>` in
scope - the next failure after 0197 in that crate.

The node now also allocates value ivars (the largest const-param count
over the candidate traits), find_method and autoderef_find_method take
them beside the type ivars, and the duplicate-trait collapse in
expr_cs.cpp fills them in the same way instead of its TODO.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

